{"study_accession":"PRJNA996938","secondary_study_accession":"SRP450584","title":"CD14 Serves as a Predicted Marker for Coronary Artery Lesions in Kawasaki Disease","description":"Kawasaki Disease (KD) is an acute vasculitis that commonly occurs in younger children, which can lead to coronary artery aneurysm, dilatation and other severe cardiovascular diseases. However, the mechanism of coronary artery lesions remains unclear. In this study, we detected the mRNA expression profile of KD patients in the acute and subacute stages in the coronary artery lesions group (KD-CALs) and the non-coronary artery lesions group (KD-nCALs). 62 differentially expressed genes were found in the CALs group, and the differential genes were enriched in immune-related signaling pathways, significantly in the NF-kappa B signaling pathway. CD14-mRNA was confirmed to be down-regulated in the subacute stage of KD-CALs. Moreover, the downregulation of CD14 caused a decrease in the expression of a series of downstream genes such as IκBα, A20, and A1/Bf1_1. But only the downregulation of IκBα was in sync with CD14. In conclusion, CD14-mRNA was differentially expressed in the KD-CALs group and regulated the expression of IκBα via the NF-kappa B signaling pathway, finally inducing vascular endothelial cell injury. It can be served as a predicted marker for coronary artery lesions in KD. Besides, CD14 could become a potential therapy target for KD, especially in reversing coronary artery lesions (CALs). Overall design: We enrolled 12 children diagnosed with KD, and studied the transcriptome differences between KD patients in the acute and subacute stages in the coronary artery lesions group (KD-CALs) and the non-coronary artery lesions group (KD-nCALs). Then, qRT-PCR was used to validate the difference. Meanwhile, we enrolled 12 new KD patients (6 of KD-CALs, and 6 of KD-nCALs; Each group collected blood samples from acute and subacute periods, respectively) and investigated the expression of CD14 and a series of downstream genes in NF-Kappa B Signaling Pathway (such as A20, A1/Bf1_1, and IκBα) by qRT-PCR. At last, molecular docking was used to analyze the binding force of the core effective compounds with CD14 in the “herbal medicine-compound-target” network.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":24,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN36660607","study_accession":"PRJNA996938","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"KD-nCALs, subacute stage 202135B","description":"KD-nCALs, subacute stage 202135B","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7655311","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-06-29","attributes":[["source_name","PBMC"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR25372902","experiment_accession":"SRX21112255","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":27295396,"base_count":8188618800,"first_public":"2026-06-29","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM7655311: KD-nCALs, subacute stage 202135B Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN36660608","study_accession":"PRJNA996938","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"KD-nCALs, subacute stage 202134B","description":"KD-nCALs, subacute stage 202134B","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7655310","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-06-29","attributes":[["source_name","PBMC"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR25372903","experiment_accession":"SRX21112254","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":26120399,"base_count":7836119700,"first_public":"2026-06-29","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM7655310: KD-nCALs, subacute stage 202134B Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN36660609